sored surveys' tighter numbers could move this into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat pits Democrat Peggy Flanagan against Republican Michele Tafoya after Tina Smith's retirement. Polling throughout October has consistently shown Flanagan ahead, with nonpartisan surveys from KSTP/SurveyUSA and the New York Times/Siena showing leads of seven to fourteen points, while Republican-leaning pollsters show a tighter three-to-four-point race. Most expert raters call the race Likely or Lean Democratic, and prediction markets price Flanagan's chances around ninety percent.\n\nTafoya has raised comparable money to Flanagan, but Flanagan has drawn far more outside support while also absorbing heavy outside opposition spending. The state's modest Democratic lean and a favorable national environment for Democrats this cycle give Flanagan the edge, though the gap between partisan pollsters leaves some room for a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7758, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8073, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7878, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7863, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.738, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7059, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7067, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8031, "margin": 